# 5. FREQUENCY BANDS

Common Wi-Fi bands include:

- 2.4 GHz
- 5 GHz
- 6 GHz

General characteristics:

### 2.4 GHz
- Longer range
- More congestion
- Fewer non-overlapping channels in many deployments

### 5 GHz
- More channels
- Generally less crowded than 2.4 GHz
- Shorter range than 2.4 GHz in many environments

### 6 GHz
- Additional spectrum for supported Wi-Fi generations
- Requires compatible equipment

