# 15. WPA/WPA2 PASSWORD SECURITY

For PSK-based Wi-Fi, security depends heavily on the strength of the password/passphrase.

Conceptually:

```text
Captured authentication material
          ↓
Offline password testing
          ↓
Candidate password
          ↓
Cryptographic verification
```

A weak password is much more vulnerable to guessing than a strong random one.

---

# 16. DEFENSE AGAINST PASSWORD GUESSING

Use:

- Strong random passphrases
- WPA2/WPA3
- Enterprise authentication where appropriate
- Avoid shared credentials when practical
- Monitoring
- Credential rotation according to policy

